1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,862
What if the stars traced your movements?

2
00:00:02,902 --> 00:00:04,387
You walk home at night,

3
00:00:04,427 --> 00:00:05,713
and with every step,

4
00:00:05,753 --> 00:00:07,768
a new star blinks on above you,

5
00:00:07,808 --> 00:00:10,685
connected to the last by a thin golden line.

6
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:15,261
Soon the whole town is looking up.

7
00:00:15,301 --> 00:00:17,750
The sky is covered in glowing paths.

8
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:20,377
Bakers' loops, mail carriers' zigzags,

9
00:00:20,417 --> 00:00:23,972
and one very tangled spot that belongs to a toddler.

10
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:25,480
You try to hide.

11
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:27,153
You duck into a basement,

12
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:29,762
and your star hovers over the roof like

13
00:00:29,802 --> 00:00:30,966
a patient firefly.

14
00:00:31,006 --> 00:00:33,106
The sky can't see through walls,

15
00:00:33,146 --> 00:00:35,247
but it remembers where you went.

16
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:38,947
Lying doesn't work either.

17
00:00:38,987 --> 00:00:40,643
I stayed home all night,

18
00:00:40,683 --> 00:00:42,127
you tell your friend,

19
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:45,165
while the sky quietly draws three ice cream

20
00:00:45,205 --> 00:00:46,225
cones in a row.

21
00:00:46,265 --> 00:00:49,334
Your friend raises one very patient eyebrow.

22
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:51,354
Astronomers get excited.

23
00:00:51,394 --> 00:00:54,121
Constellations are no longer ancient myths.

24
00:00:54,161 --> 00:00:56,244
Orion is just a man who walks his

25
00:00:56,284 --> 00:00:57,402
dog every evening.

26
00:00:57,442 --> 00:00:59,140
In this thought experiment,

27
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:01,263
the sky becomes a gigantic diary.

28
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:03,950
At night, a child asks a question:

29
00:01:03,990 --> 00:01:05,201
who is watching us?

30
00:01:05,241 --> 00:01:07,441
An old telescope shows the answer.

31
00:01:07,481 --> 00:01:07,902
Nobody.

32
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:09,614
The stars aren't watching.

33
00:01:09,654 --> 00:01:11,920
They're simply keeping you company,

34
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,171
like quiet friends.

35
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:14,751
Here's the twist.

36
00:01:14,791 --> 00:01:16,160
When the child walks,

37
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,569
the stars drift down,

38
00:01:17,609 --> 00:01:20,722
one by one, to hover beside her like fireflies.

39
00:01:20,762 --> 00:01:22,668
They aren't tracing her path.

40
00:01:22,708 --> 00:01:25,151
They've just been following her home.

41
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:28,554
So tonight, when you walk under the sky,

42
00:01:28,594 --> 00:01:30,669
don't worry about being watched.

43
00:01:30,709 --> 00:01:31,925
Wave at your stars.

44
00:01:31,965 --> 00:01:35,296
Somewhere above, a thousand tiny lights are happily

45
00:01:35,336 --> 00:01:38,667
drawing your whole life as one long, shining heart.
